10
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,980
Guess what? The worst food I ever had was in France.

11
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,200
Really? That's odd.

12
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:52,020
I thought the French were all good cooks.

13
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,380
Yes, that's right.

14
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,400
I suppose it's really like anywhere else though.

15
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:01,520
You know, some places are good, some bad, but it's really all our own fault.

16
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:02,780
What do you mean?

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:05,640
Well, it was the first time I'd been to France.

18
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,080
This was years ago when I was at school.

19
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:12,220
I went there with my parents' friends from my father's school.

20
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:15,120
They'd hired a coach to take them to Switzerland.

21
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:16,540
A school trip?

22
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:20,180
Right. Most of them had never been abroad before.

23
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:25,360
We'd crossed the English Channel at night and we set off through France.

24
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:30,200
And breakfast time arrived and the coach driver had arranged for us to stop at this

25
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:35,640
little café. There we all were, tired and hungry, and then we made the great

26
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,900
discovery. What was that?

27
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,360
Bacon and eggs.

28
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,420
Fantastic! The real English breakfast.

29
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,360
Yes. Anyway, we didn't know any better.

30
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:48,180
So we had it and...

31
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:49,660
What was it like?

32
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,980
Disgusting? Oh, it was incredible.

33
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,280
They just got a bowl and put some fat in it.

34
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:59,920
And then they put some bacon in the fat, broke an egg over the top, and put the

35
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:02,260
whole lot in the oven for about ten minutes.

36
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:03,600
In the oven?

37
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,640
You're joking. You can't cook bacon and eggs in oven.

38
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:09,760
Well, they must have done it that way.

39
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:12,220
It was hot, but it wasn't cooked.

40
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:17,100
There was just this egg floating about in gallons of fat and raw bacon.

41
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,200
Did you actually eat it?

42
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:23,260
nobody did. They all wanted to turn round and go home.

43
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,380
You know, back to tea bags and fish and chips.

44
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,360
You can't blame them, really.

45
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:32,100
Anyway, the next night we were all given another foreign speciality.

46
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:33,840
What was that?

47
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,960
Snails. That really finished them off.

48
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,680
Lovely holiday that was.

