00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:01,520
are famous for carrying things around.

98
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:07,460
Some, like homing pigeons, can be trained to deliver messages and packages.

99
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:12,940
Other birds unknowingly carry seeds that cling to them for the ride.

100
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:20,680
Canadian scientists have found a worrisome new example of the power that birds have

101
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,040
to spread stuff around.

102
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:28,800
Way up north in the Canadian Arctic, seabirds are picking up dangerous chemicals in

103
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:32,980
the ocean and delivering them to ponds near where the birds live.

104
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:40,260
Some 10,000 pairs of the birds, called fulmars, a kind of Arctic seabird, make their

105
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:43,660
nests on Devon Island, north of the Arctic Circle.

106
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:50,460
The fulmars travel some 400 kilometers over the sea to find food.

107
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:56,620
When they return home, their droppings end up all around their nesting sites,

108
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,860
including in nearby ponds.

109
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:05,360
Previously, scientists noticed pollutants arriving in the Arctic with the wind.

110
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:11,200
Salmon also carry dangerous chemicals as the fish migrate between rivers and the

111
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:17,260
sea. The bodies of fish and other meat -eaters can build up high levels of the

112
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:23,600
chemicals. To test the polluting power of fulmars, researchers collected samples of

113
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:27,000
deposit from 11 ponds on Devon Island.

114
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:32,920
In ponds closest to the colony, the results showed there were far more pollutants

115
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:35,660
than in ponds less affected by the birds.

116
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:41,800
The pollutants in the ponds appear to come from fish that fulmars eat when they're

117
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,000
out on the ocean.

118
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:48,740
People who live, hunt, or fish near bird colonies need to be careful, the

119
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:54,120
researchers say. The birds don't mean to cause harm, but the chemicals they carry

120
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:56,380
can cause major problems.

