201
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:37,740
Today, we're going to be talking about becoming a social worker.

202
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:40,960
Social work is the helping profession.

203
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:47,540
Its primary mission is to enhance human well -being and help meet the basic needs of

204
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:53,340
all people, with a particular focus on those who are vulnerable, oppressed and

205
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,560
living in poverty.

206
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,820
We often deal with complex human needs.

207
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:03,660
Social work is different from other professions because we focus on the person and

208
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:10,940
environment. deal with the external factors that impact a person's and outlook, and

209
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:16,180
we create opportunity for assessment and intervention to help clients and

210
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:21,540
communities cope effectively with the reality and change that reality when

211
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:28,880
necessary. In thousands of ways, social workers help other people, people from every

212
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:35,720
age, every background across the country, wherever needed, social workers come to

213
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:42,020
help. The most well aspect of the profession is that of a social safety net.

214
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:47,880
We help guide people to critical resources and counsel them on life -changing

215
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:53,780
decisions. There are more than 600,000 professional social workers in the country,

216
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:59,420
and we all either have a bachelor's degree, a master's degree or a Ph.D.

217
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,460
in social work.

218
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:05,220
There are more clinically trained social workers than clinically trained

219
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:10,020
psychiatrists, psychologists and psychiatric nurses combined.

220
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:15,460
Throughout this series, you will learn more about the profession, the necessary

221
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:21,300
steps to get a social work degree, the rich history of social work and the many ways

222
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:23,200
that social workers help others.

223
